# Deny-by-default build context: everything is excluded, then the files a
# Dockerfile copies are allowed back in. This is deliberate — it keeps the
# context small (no .git, no build/, no test fixtures) and makes every future
# addition an explicit decision. The cost is drift: a new package that reaches
# a binary must be added BOTH here and to that Dockerfile's COPY list, or the
# image build breaks. The CI `dockerbuild` job builds both images on main
# pushes and pull requests to catch exactly that.
*
!cmd/krot-cp/
!cmd/krot-agent/
!internal/store/
!internal/model/
!internal/render/
!internal/staticmerge/
!internal/authentik/
!internal/directory/
!internal/zitadel/
!internal/oidc/
!internal/sub/
!internal/web/
!internal/cpapi/
!internal/agentapi/
!internal/upstream/
!internal/rebuild/
!go.mod
!go.sum
!LICENSE
!licenses/
